    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes owner responses include a `displayName` field formatted as `'LastName, FirstName'`, computed from the stored names.\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n   This computes the value from the stored `lastName`/`firstName`. Because both the create responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and the GET responder (`RespondWithOwner`) map through `toOwnerDto`, the field is present consistently.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` which creates an owner and asserts `$.displayName` equals `\"LastName, John\"`.",
